{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789028433,"nonce":"wzwAcCMjxwmDSe8mg7jVqYXEFBU=","message":"Narrowed a long way by instrumentation. Recording it all, because the surprising part is structural rather than about this bug.\n\nWHERE IT IS NOT:\n* Not the arithmetic. Comparing two UI8 registers directly (no widening) gives\n  the right answer under --mode jit; the bits are 0x90 as they should be.\n* Not printing or call marshalling. `(e : Int) \u003e 128` is false under --mode\n  jit, so the fault reaches control flow.\n* Not Opcode::ToInt's LLVM lowering, which tests src_kind and zero-extends.\n* Not cast_for_call, which zero-extends int-to-int.\n\nTHE STRUCTURAL FINDING. A probe at the top of translate_opcode counts:\n\n    hybrid (promoting)   23 calls\n    AOT                  4385 calls\n    --mode jit           0 calls\n\n--mode jit is the CRANELIFT-first path -- 'compile reached functions with\nCranelift, then promote them to LLVM' -- so none of opcode.rs covers it. Every\nnull guard and cast fix in that file applies to hybrid and AOT only. Worth\nknowing well beyond this issue.\n\nTHE LIKELY SITE. cranelift/lower.rs:586 `coerce` widens with an unconditional\n`sextend`, under the comment 'HashLink integers are signed; widening preserves\nthe value.' That is false for HUI8 and HUI16, which HashLink widens with MOVZX\n-- 144 sign-extends to -112 and 255 to -1, matching every observed failure, and\nonly for values with the high bit set, which is why the two cases yielding 0\nagreed.\n\nPatching Opcode::ToInt alone to use uextend did NOT fix it, so the widening\nthat reaches the output comes through one of coerce's other 13 call sites --\nthe field load at 639 and the call-argument paths at 434/578 are the\ncandidates. That change was reverted rather than left in unverified.\n\nTHE FIX is therefore coerce itself: it decides signedness without knowing the\nHL kind, so signedness has to become explicit at all 14 sites rather than\nassumed at one. reg_kind(r) already exists for it.","files":null}]}